      "The trade-offs are reach and capability. iOS historically lags on PWA features (limited push, install quirks), so coverage isn't uniform. Service workers add real complexity — caching bugs and the update lifecycle are notorious sources of 'why are users seeing old code?' incidents. And a PWA still can't match a native app's deepest device integration. The decision is usually PWA when broad reach, instant updates, and offline-ish behaviour matter more than the last 10% of native power.",
