    bigPicture: "A PWA is the convergence point of several web ideas: the service worker is a programmable layer over the network, Cache Storage and IndexedDB provide its offline data, the manifest plugs into the OS, and HTTPS underpins the whole thing. It builds directly on web storage and offline-first thinking, and it's how a web app climbs toward the territory the native Flutter app occupies — same goals (offline, installable, push), reached from the browser side.",
