    scale: "When learning, a PWA is a manifest plus a tiny service worker that caches a few files — enough to earn the install prompt. In production you adopt a proven caching library (Workbox), pick strategies per resource type, handle updates gracefully, and test offline behaviour as a real feature. At enterprise scale, the service worker becomes load-bearing infrastructure: versioned caches, careful cache invalidation tied to deploys, push-notification campaigns, and monitoring for stale-version incidents. At planet scale, PWAs serve as the low-bandwidth front door for emerging markets (think 'Lite' apps) — engineered to install small, run offline by default, sync opportunistically, and degrade gracefully across an enormous range of devices and network conditions worldwide.",
